{"source":"Gulati 等 - 2021 - 2021 AHAACCASECHESTSAEMSCCTSCMR Guideline for the Evaluation and Diagnosis of Chest Pain A Re.pdf","page":11,"pageWidth":585,"pageHeight":783,"items":[{"text":"November 30, 2021","rect":[75.8,24,143.9672,32],"fontSize":8},{"text":"Circulation","rect":[278.288,24,312.08000000000004,32],"fontSize":8},{"text":".","rect":[312.08000000000004,24,313.41600000000005,32],"fontSize":8},{"text":"2021;144:e368–e454. DOI: 10.1161/CIR.0000000000001029","rect":[315.58400000000006,24,535.5015999999999,32],"fontSize":8},{"text":"e378","rect":[49.49600000000001,24.048,67.16000000000001,32.048],"fontSize":8},{"text":"Gulati et al","rect":[49.5,751.5,85.50000000000001,759.5],"fontSize":8},{"text":"2021 Chest Pain Guideline","rect":[444.5,751.5,535.4992000000001,759.5],"fontSize":8},{"text":"CLINICAL STATEMENTS","rect":[17.15,631.5866,99.47840000000039,642.5866],"fontSize":9.9},{"text":"AND GUIDELINES","rect":[28.15,641.7887,90.0745000000004,652.7887],"fontSize":9.9},{"text":"2.1.1. A Focus on the Uniqueness of Chest Pain","rect":[49.5,715.5,261.35,725.5],"fontSize":10},{"text":"in","rect":[49.5,703.5,57.620000000000005,713.5],"fontSize":10},{"text":"Women","rect":[60.330000000000005,703.5,93.86000000000001,713.5],"fontSize":10},{"text":"Recommendations for a Focus on the Uniqueness of Chest Pain","rect":[53.75,689.3178,257.01529999999997,696.3178],"fontSize":7},{"text":"in","rect":[53.75,680.3158000000001,59.434,687.3158000000001],"fontSize":7},{"text":"Women","rect":[61.330999999999996,680.3158000000001,84.949,687.3158000000001],"fontSize":7},{"text":"Referenced studies that support the recommendations are","rect":[53.75,671.3138000000001,239.3809,678.3138000000001],"fontSize":7},{"text":"summarized in Online Data Supplements 3 and 4.","rect":[53.75,662.3118000000002,211.36829999999998,669.3118000000002],"fontSize":7},{"text":"COR","rect":[61.961,648.2558000000001,77.277,655.2558000000001],"fontSize":7},{"text":"LOE","rect":[101.69999999999999,648.2558000000001,115.41999999999999,655.2558000000001],"fontSize":7},{"text":"Recommendations","rect":[131.63199999999998,648.2558000000001,191.265,655.2558000000001],"fontSize":7},{"text":"1","rect":[67.65199999999997,625.4988000000002,71.58599999999997,632.4988000000002],"fontSize":7},{"text":"B-NR","rect":[99.66999999999997,625.4988000000002,117.45699999999997,632.4988000000002],"fontSize":7},{"text":"1.","rect":[132.13599999999997,634.3468000000001,137.38599999999997,641.3468000000001],"fontSize":7},{"text":"Women who present with chest pain are at","rect":[142.13899999999995,634.3468000000001,266.5842999999999,641.3468000000001],"fontSize":7},{"text":"risk for underdiagnosis, and potential cardiac","rect":[142.13899999999995,625.3448000000002,272.3949999999999,632.3448000000002],"fontSize":7},{"text":"causes should always be considered.","rect":[142.13899999999995,616.3428000000002,249.62399999999997,623.3428000000002],"fontSize":7},{"text":"1-7","rect":[249.6203,618.6836,255.82342,622.7646],"fontSize":4.081},{"text":"1","rect":[67.6535,588.9736,71.58749999999999,595.9736],"fontSize":7},{"text":"B-NR","rect":[99.6715,588.9736,117.45849999999999,595.9736],"fontSize":7},{"text":"2.","rect":[132.1375,602.5466,137.3875,609.5466],"fontSize":7},{"text":"In women presenting with chest pain, it","rect":[142.14049999999997,602.5466,255.49079999999998,609.5466],"fontSize":7},{"text":"is recommended to obtain a history that","rect":[142.14049999999997,593.5446000000001,257.6685,600.5446000000001],"fontSize":7},{"text":"emphasizes accompanying symptoms that","rect":[142.14049999999997,584.5426000000001,264.7945,591.5426000000001],"fontSize":7},{"text":"are","rect":[142.14049999999997,575.5406000000002,151.47849999999997,582.5406000000002],"fontSize":7},{"text":"more common in women with ACS.","rect":[153.37549999999996,575.5406000000002,255.49709999999993,582.5406000000002],"fontSize":7},{"text":"1-7","rect":[255.4933,577.8755,261.69642,581.9565],"fontSize":4.081},{"text":"Synopsis","rect":[301.5,713.4734,346.4928,725.4734],"fontSize":10.8},{"text":"Most patients who present to the ED with chest pain are","rect":[301.5,697.4734,535.4800000000001,707.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"women, particularly among those","rect":[301.5,685.4734,438.59000000000026,695.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"≥","rect":[441.03000000000003,685.4734,446.52000000000004,695.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"65 years of age.","rect":[446.55,685.4734,513.9050000000001,695.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"8","rect":[513.9463,688.8034,517.34519,694.6334],"fontSize":5.83},{"text":"The","rect":[519.7642999999999,685.4734,535.5043,695.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"ISCHEMIA (International Study of Comparative Health","rect":[301.50429999999994,673.4734,535.5033000000002,683.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"Effectiveness With Medical and Invasive Approaches)","rect":[301.50429999999994,661.4734,535.5243000000003,671.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"trial demonstrated that women with moderate-to-severe","rect":[301.50429999999994,649.4734,535.5143000000003,659.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"ischemia are more symptomatic than men.","rect":[301.50429999999994,637.4734,480.42930000000035,647.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"9","rect":[480.4725,640.8034,483.87139,646.6334],"fontSize":5.83},{"text":"Women are","rect":[487.01550000000003,637.4734,535.4994999999999,647.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"less likely to have timely and appropriate care.","rect":[301.50050000000005,625.4734,506.88050000000067,635.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"10","rect":[506.9084,628.8034,513.73533,634.6334],"fontSize":5.83},{"text":"This","rect":[518.2643,625.4734,535.5043,635.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"could be explained by the fact that women are more like-","rect":[301.50430000000006,613.4734,535.5043000000004,623.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"ly to experience prodromal symptoms when they seek","rect":[301.50430000000006,601.4734,535.5243000000004,611.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"medical care.","rect":[301.50430000000006,589.4734,356.46430000000015,599.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"11","rect":[356.5116,592.8034,363.33853,598.6334],"fontSize":5.83},{"text":"Women may also present with accompa-","rect":[365.89759999999995,589.4734,535.4875999999999,599.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"nying symptoms (eg, nausea, fatigue, and shortness of","rect":[301.4976,577.4734,535.5176000000004,587.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"breath) more often than men.","rect":[301.4976,565.4734,428.9376000000003,575.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"12-14","rect":[428.9814,568.8034,444.75738000000007,574.6334],"fontSize":5.83},{"text":"However, chest pain","rect":[448.6363,565.4734,535.5043,575.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"remains the predominant symptom reported by women","rect":[301.49629999999996,553.4734,535.5163000000006,563.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"among those ultimately diagnosed with ACS, occurring","rect":[301.49629999999996,541.4734,535.4763000000003,551.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"with a frequency equal to men.","rect":[301.49629999999996,529.4734,430.2763000000002,539.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"3,5-7,15,16","rect":[430.3285,532.8034,458.5521130000002,538.6334],"fontSize":5.83},{"text":"Recommendation-Specific Supportive Text","rect":[301.5,493.4734,510.0372000000001,505.4734],"fontSize":10.8},{"text":"1.","rect":[311.5,477.4734,319.05,487.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"Traditional risk score tools and physician assess-","rect":[326,477.4734,535.4900000000002,487.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"ments often underestimate risk in women and","rect":[326,465.4734,535.4900000000002,475.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"misclassify","rect":[326,453.4734,371.48000000000013,463.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"them","rect":[377.63000000000005,453.4734,398.8300000000001,463.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"as","rect":[404.9800000000001,453.4734,414.61000000000007,463.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"having","rect":[420.7600000000001,453.4734,448.10000000000014,463.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"nonischemic","rect":[454.25000000000017,453.4734,506.6300000000003,463.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"chest","rect":[512.7800000000002,453.4734,535.4900000000001,463.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"pain.","rect":[326,441.4734,345.37000000000006,451.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"1,2","rect":[345.4198,444.8034,353.24949000000004,450.6334],"fontSize":5.83},{"text":"The PROMISE (Prospective Multicenter","rect":[359.04839999999996,441.4734,535.5174,451.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"Imaging Study for Evaluation of Chest Pain) trial","rect":[325.99839999999995,429.4734,535.5284000000001,439.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"looked at sex differences in the presentation, risk","rect":[325.99839999999995,417.4734,535.5284000000004,427.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"factors, demographics, noninvasive test referrals,","rect":[325.99839999999995,405.4734,535.4984000000001,415.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"and results of 10","rect":[325.99839999999995,393.4734,397.9384000000002,403.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"003 stable outpatients with sus-","rect":[399.29839999999996,393.4734,535.4884000000002,403.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"pected CAD.","rect":[325.99839999999995,381.4734,380.74840000000006,391.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"1","rect":[380.7982,384.8034,384.19709,390.6334],"fontSize":5.83},{"text":"Women commonly presented with","rect":[388.4962,381.4734,535.5062,391.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"chest pain symptoms similar to men but also had","rect":[325.9962,369.4734,535.4662000000002,379.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"a greater prevalence of other symptoms such as","rect":[325.9962,357.4734,535.5162000000003,367.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"palpitations, jaw and neck pain, as well as back","rect":[325.9962,345.4734,535.5262000000002,355.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"pain. Women also had more cardiovascular risk","rect":[325.9962,333.4734,535.5062,343.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"factors,","rect":[325.9962,321.4734,356.7762000000001,331.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"including","rect":[363.85620000000006,321.4734,401.54620000000017,331.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"hypertension","rect":[408.62120000000004,321.4734,462.7212000000002,331.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"(66.6%","rect":[469.8012,321.4734,501.30120000000005,331.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"versus","rect":[508.3762,321.4734,535.5061999999998,331.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"63.2%;","rect":[325.9962,309.4734,356.23620000000005,319.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"P","rect":[363.2262,309.4734,369.5262,319.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"<0.001),","rect":[369.57620000000003,309.4734,406.38620000000014,319.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"hyperlipidemia","rect":[413.3762000000001,309.4734,473.81620000000026,319.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"(68.9%","rect":[480.80620000000005,309.4734,512.3052000000001,319.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"ver-","rect":[519.2952,309.4734,535.4951999999998,319.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"sus 66.3%;","rect":[325.99620000000004,297.4734,374.4162000000001,307.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"P","rect":[377.9162,297.4734,384.2162,307.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"=0.004), older age (62.4±7.9 years","rect":[384.2162,297.4734,535.4762000000001,307.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"of age versus 59.0±8.4 years of age,","rect":[325.99620000000004,285.4734,488.4262000000002,295.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"P","rect":[492.31620000000004,285.4734,498.61620000000005,295.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"<0.001),","rect":[498.68620000000004,285.4734,535.4961999999998,295.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"cerebral or peripheral artery disease (6.2% ver-","rect":[325.99620000000004,273.4734,535.5062000000003,283.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"sus 4.7%;","rect":[325.99620000000004,261.4734,368.7562000000001,271.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"P","rect":[372.68620000000004,261.4734,378.98620000000005,271.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"<0.001), family history of premature","rect":[379.03620000000006,261.4734,535.5062000000001,271.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"CAD (34.6% versus 29.3%;","rect":[325.99620000000004,249.47340000000003,446.35620000000023,259.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"P","rect":[450.2862000000001,249.47340000000003,456.58620000000013,259.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"<0.001), and sed-","rect":[456.62620000000004,249.47340000000003,535.5061999999999,259.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"entary lifestyle (53.5% versus 43.4%;","rect":[325.99620000000004,237.47340000000003,488.40620000000035,247.47340000000003],"fontSize":10},{"text":"P","rect":[492.35620000000006,237.47340000000003,498.65620000000007,247.47340000000003],"fontSize":10},{"text":"<0.001).","rect":[498.68620000000004,237.47340000000003,535.4961999999998,247.47340000000003],"fontSize":10},{"text":"Physician","rect":[325.99620000000004,225.47340000000003,365.96620000000013,235.47340000000003],"fontSize":10},{"text":"assessments","rect":[372.16620000000006,225.47340000000003,426.8262000000002,235.47340000000003],"fontSize":10},{"text":"often","rect":[433.0262,225.47340000000003,454.90620000000007,235.47340000000003],"fontSize":10},{"text":"misclassify","rect":[461.1062,225.47340000000003,506.58620000000013,235.47340000000003],"fontSize":10},{"text":"chest","rect":[512.7862,225.47340000000003,535.4961999999999,235.47340000000003],"fontSize":10},{"text":"pain","rect":[325.99620000000004,213.47340000000003,343.6462000000001,223.47340000000003],"fontSize":10},{"text":"as","rect":[351.91620000000006,213.47340000000003,361.54620000000006,223.47340000000003],"fontSize":10},{"text":"nonanginal.","rect":[369.8162000000001,213.47340000000003,417.6162000000002,223.47340000000003],"fontSize":10},{"text":"The","rect":[425.88620000000014,213.47340000000003,441.62620000000015,223.47340000000003],"fontSize":10},{"text":"BARI","rect":[449.8962000000002,213.47340000000003,472.34620000000024,223.47340000000003],"fontSize":10},{"text":"2D","rect":[480.6162000000003,213.47340000000003,493.37620000000027,223.47340000000003],"fontSize":10},{"text":"(Bypass","rect":[501.6462000000003,213.47340000000003,535.4862000000002,223.47340000000003],"fontSize":10},{"text":"Angioplasty","rect":[325.99620000000004,201.47340000000003,375.0362000000002,211.47340000000003],"fontSize":10},{"text":"Revascularization","rect":[384.6462000000001,201.47340000000003,457.53620000000024,211.47340000000003],"fontSize":10},{"text":"Investigation","rect":[467.14620000000014,201.47340000000003,520.0462000000002,211.47340000000003],"fontSize":10},{"text":"2","rect":[529.6562000000001,201.47340000000003,535.4862000000002,211.47340000000003],"fontSize":10},{"text":"Diabetes) trial reported that women with diabetes","rect":[325.99620000000004,189.47340000000003,535.4762000000004,199.47340000000003],"fontSize":10},{"text":"had a higher prevalence of angina than their male","rect":[325.99620000000004,177.47340000000003,535.5262000000002,187.47340000000003],"fontSize":10},{"text":"counterparts, with a lower functional capacity and","rect":[325.99620000000004,165.47340000000003,535.4762000000003,175.47340000000003],"fontSize":10},{"text":"a lower incidence of obstructive CAD.","rect":[325.99620000000004,153.47340000000003,483.89620000000036,163.47340000000003],"fontSize":10},{"text":"16","rect":[483.9477,156.8034,490.77463,162.63340000000002],"fontSize":5.83},{"text":"2.","rect":[311.5,141.4734,318.95,151.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"In the VIRGO (Variation in Recovery: Role of Gender","rect":[326,141.4734,535.5139999999999,151.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"on Outcomes of Young AMI Patients) study, men","rect":[326,129.4734,535.4799999999998,139.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"and women","rect":[326,117.4734,373.9649999999999,127.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"≤","rect":[376.59000000000003,117.4734,382.08000000000004,127.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"55 years of age were equally likely to","rect":[382.03000000000003,117.4734,535.5029999999999,127.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"present with chest pain (defined as pain, pressure,","rect":[326,105.4734,535.5199999999998,115.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"tightness, discomfort; 89.5% versus 87%, respec-","rect":[326,93.4734,535.49,103.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"tively). Women were more likely to report","rect":[326,81.4734,490.37999999999994,91.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"≥","rect":[492.5499999999995,81.4734,498.0399999999995,91.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"3 associ-","rect":[498.02,81.4734,535.5000000000002,91.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"ated symptoms than men (eg, epigastric symptoms,","rect":[326,69.4734,535.4999999999999,79.4734],"fontSize":10},{"text":"Table 3.","rect":[49.625,525.8,77.649,533.8],"fontSize":8},{"text":"Chest Pain Characteristics and Corresponding Causes","rect":[85.32900000000001,525.8,283.385,533.8],"fontSize":8},{"text":"Nature","rect":[53.75,509.5,73.735,516.5],"fontSize":7},{"text":"Anginal symptoms are perceived as retrosternal chest discomfort (eg, pain,","rect":[53.75,495.647,275.5919,502.647],"fontSize":7},{"text":"discomfort, heaviness, tightness, pressure, constriction, squeezing) (Section","rect":[53.75,486.645,279.241,493.645],"fontSize":7},{"text":"1.4.2, Defining Chest Pain).","rect":[53.75,477.643,135.846,484.643],"fontSize":7},{"text":"Sharp chest pain that increases with inspiration and lying supine is unlikely","rect":[53.75,463.78999999999996,274.39699999999993,470.78999999999996],"fontSize":7},{"text":"related to ischemic heart disease (eg, these symptoms usually occur with","rect":[53.75,454.78799999999995,270.3433,461.78799999999995],"fontSize":7},{"text":"acute pericarditis).","rect":[53.75,445.78599999999994,108.735,452.78599999999994],"fontSize":7},{"text":"Onset and duration","rect":[53.75,431.93299999999994,111.21300000000001,438.93299999999994],"fontSize":7},{"text":"Anginal symptoms gradually build in intensity over a few minutes.","rect":[53.75,418.0799999999999,245.50799999999998,425.0799999999999],"fontSize":7},{"text":"Sudden onset of ripping chest pain (with radiation to the upper or lower back)","rect":[53.75,404.2269999999999,276.2730000000005,411.2269999999999],"fontSize":7},{"text":"is unlikely to be anginal and is suspicious of an acute aortic syndrome.","rect":[53.75,395.2249999999999,254.11100000000064,402.2249999999999],"fontSize":7},{"text":"Fleeting chest pain—of few seconds’ duration—is unlikely to be related to","rect":[53.75,381.3719999999999,267.41799999999995,388.3719999999999],"fontSize":7},{"text":"ischemic heart disease.","rect":[53.75,372.3699999999999,123.176,379.3699999999999],"fontSize":7},{"text":"Location and radiation","rect":[53.75,358.5169999999999,119.67600000000002,365.5169999999999],"fontSize":7},{"text":"Pain that can be localized to a very limited area and pain radiating to below","rect":[53.75,344.6639999999999,275.27899999999994,351.6639999999999],"fontSize":7},{"text":"the umbilicus or hip are unlikely related to myocardial ischemia.","rect":[53.75,335.66199999999986,239.84290000000004,342.66199999999986],"fontSize":7},{"text":"Severity","rect":[53.75,321.80899999999986,77.522,328.80899999999986],"fontSize":7},{"text":"Ripping chest pain (“worse chest pain of my life”), especially when sudden","rect":[53.75,307.95599999999985,274.40329999999994,314.95599999999985],"fontSize":7},{"text":"in onset and occurring in a hypertensive patient, or with a known bicuspid","rect":[53.75,298.95399999999984,271.63899999999995,305.95399999999984],"fontSize":7},{"text":"aortic valve or aortic dilation, is suspicious of an acute aortic syndrome (eg,","rect":[53.75,289.9519999999998,276.17499999999995,296.9519999999998],"fontSize":7},{"text":"aortic dissection).","rect":[53.75,280.9499999999998,106.404,287.9499999999998],"fontSize":7},{"text":"Precipitating factors","rect":[53.75,267.0969999999998,113.55100000000002,274.0969999999998],"fontSize":7},{"text":"Physical exercise or emotional stress are common triggers of anginal","rect":[53.75,253.2439999999998,268.65700000000055,260.2439999999998],"fontSize":7},{"text":"symptoms.","rect":[53.75,244.2419999999998,87.08399999999997,251.2419999999998],"fontSize":7},{"text":"Occurrence at rest or with minimal exertion associated with anginal symp-","rect":[53.75,230.38899999999978,272.241,237.38899999999978],"fontSize":7},{"text":"toms usually indicates ACS.","rect":[53.75,221.38699999999977,136.8813,228.38699999999977],"fontSize":7},{"text":"Positional chest pain is usually nonischemic (eg, musculoskeletal).","rect":[53.75,207.53399999999976,249.18789999999998,214.53399999999976],"fontSize":7},{"text":"Relieving factors","rect":[53.75,193.68099999999976,103.044,200.68099999999976],"fontSize":7},{"text":"Relief with nitroglycerin is not necessarily diagnostic of myocardial ischemia","rect":[53.75,179.82799999999975,277.76120000000003,186.82799999999975],"fontSize":7},{"text":"and should not be used as a diagnostic criterion.","rect":[53.75,170.82599999999974,198.27899999999997,177.82599999999974],"fontSize":7},{"text":"Associated symptoms","rect":[53.75,156.97299999999973,119.22800000000001,163.97299999999973],"fontSize":7},{"text":"Common symptoms associated with myocardial ischemia include, but are","rect":[53.75,143.11999999999972,270.90889999999996,150.11999999999972],"fontSize":7},{"text":"not limited to, dyspnea, palpitations, diaphoresis, lightheadedness, presyn-","rect":[53.75,134.1179999999997,274.0806,141.1179999999997],"fontSize":7},{"text":"cope or syncope, upper abdominal pain, or heartburn unrelated to meals","rect":[53.75,125.11599999999972,267.85900000000004,132.1159999999997],"fontSize":7},{"text":"and nausea or vomiting.","rect":[53.75,116.11399999999972,124.19100000000002,123.11399999999972],"fontSize":7},{"text":"Symptoms on the left or right side of the chest, stabbing, sharp pain, or","rect":[53.75,102.26099999999971,264.6579,109.26099999999971],"fontSize":7},{"text":"discomfort in the throat or abdomen may occur in patients with diabetes,","rect":[53.75,93.25899999999972,268.601,100.25899999999972],"fontSize":7},{"text":"women, and elderly patients.","rect":[53.75,84.25699999999972,138.33100000000002,91.25699999999972],"fontSize":7},{"text":"ACS indicates acute coronary syndrome.","rect":[57.628,68.65399999999971,179.28100000000003,75.65399999999971],"fontSize":7}]}